WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.912
Live standalone MCP review client. Production endpoint, no authentication. Synthetic inputs only.

2
00:00:11.912 --> 00:00:18.613
Initialize the MCP connection over HTTP.

3
00:00:18.613 --> 00:00:26.875
Discover both read-only metadata validation tools.

4
00:00:26.875 --> 00:00:35.584
P1: Minimal valid skill metadata. Return valid=true, the dated skill ruleset, no issues and truncated=false.

5
00:00:35.584 --> 00:00:44.336
P2: Valid optional skill metadata. Accept the supplied optional string fields and metadata mapping; return valid=true.

6
00:00:44.336 --> 00:00:53.038
P3: Valid portable plugin metadata. Return valid=true and ruleset agent-plugins-1.0.0. Do not claim to inspect referenced files or the ZIP.

7
00:00:53.038 --> 00:01:01.811
P4: Valid OpenAI-native metadata. Return valid=true with the dated OpenAI metadata ruleset. Explain that this is metadata validation, not publication approval.

8
00:01:01.811 --> 00:01:15.229
P5: Correct metadata and revalidate. First report valid=false and skill.directory_mismatch; after correction report valid=true. Keep the directory unchanged.

9
00:01:15.229 --> 00:01:28.834
N1: Missing required metadata and directory mismatch. Report missing/invalid name and then a directory mismatch. Do not invent a successful result.

10
00:01:28.834 --> 00:01:42.245
N2: Malformed JSON and schema errors. Return valid=false for both: input.parse for malformed JSON, schema issues for invalid field types/version. Do not crash.

11
00:01:42.245 --> 00:02:02.218
N3: Unsupported file, URL and shell actions. Explain that this MCP only accepts supplied metadata; request pasted YAML/JSON. Do not read files, fetch URLs or execute commands. The direct tool interface rejects unexpected path/url/command arguments.

12
00:02:02.218 --> 00:02:19.800
All 8 scenarios and 13 tool calls completed. Metadata validation only; no ZIP audit or publication guarantee. Native installation and model refusal remain separate checks.
